    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d32">

                <pb facs="0043" n="33" xml:id="pg33"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/1–1149: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Shanghai</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Cabot</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Shanghai</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-01-11">January 11,
                        1949</date>.<lb/>[Received January 11—5:52 a. m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>85. Vernacular press January 10 reports telegram appealing for peace sent to
                    Generalissimo and Mao Tse-tung by All China Federation of Shipping Guilds signed
                    by Tu Yueh-sheng, chairman. Sent Nanking 67, repeated Department 85.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Cabot</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
